  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61514,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 5,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients often present with symptoms related to an ovarian mass, or tumours may be found incidentally.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T14:42:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61515,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 5,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients present over a wide age range.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T14:42:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61516,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 5,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T14:42:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61517,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 5,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>DNA copy-number changes may be seen in the stromal fibromatous cells and (rarely) in epithelial cells {21976534; 15077125}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T14:42:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61518,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 5,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours vary widely in size. Cystadenomas exhibit smooth outer and inner surfaces; they may be septated and filled with watery fluid. Cysts &lt;&nbsp;1&nbsp;cm are designated as cortical inclusion cysts. Cystadenofibromas contain cysts surrounded by a variable amount of solid areas. Adenofibromas are typically solid and punctuated with small cysts. Surface papillomas are exophytic.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T14:42:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61519,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 5,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "<p>The epithelial lining of these tumours consists of non-stratified cuboidal or columnar cells (resembling tubal secretory or ciliated cells) in varying proportions. In some tumours, the epithelial lining is flattened and nondescript. Serous cystadenomas are predominantly cystic. Serous adenofibromas are composed of small glands and cysts in a prominent fibromatous stroma. Serous cystadenofibromas have cysts and broad and simple papillae embedded in prominent fibromatous stroma. Surface papillomas are characterized by small simple papillae. If &lt;&nbsp;10% of the total tumour volume (except for surface involvement) shows epithelial proliferation within the cysts that would otherwise qualify as serous borderline tumour, the tumour is designated as serous cystadenoma with focal epithelial proliferation {15897738; 31097112; 18156968}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-08-03T18:01:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61520,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 5,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T14:42:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
