  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61522,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 5,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> tumour with benign serous epithelium, with or without fibromatous stroma; for cystadenoma, the cysts should be &gt;&nbsp;1&nbsp;cm.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T14:42:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61523,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 5,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T14:42:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61524,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 5,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Serous cystadenomas, adenofibromas, cystadenofibromas, and surface papillomas are benign, but they may recur after incomplete excision. Tumours with focal intracystic epithelial proliferation are also considered to be benign, but data are limited. Focal epithelial proliferation on the ovarian surface, where it is exposed to the peritoneal cavity, may potentially be associated with recurrent disease {18156968}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T14:42:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]